    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $0\\leq x\\leq2\\pi$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q27",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x=\\frac12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\ \\frac{5\\pi}{6}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Sine is positive in quadrants 1 and 2.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\\\x&=\\pi-\\frac{\\pi}{6}=\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q28",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x=-\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\ \\frac{5\\pi}{4}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Cosine is negative in quadrants 2 and 3.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\pi-\\frac{\\pi}{4}=\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\\\x&=\\pi+\\frac{\\pi}{4}=\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q29",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan x=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\ \\frac{5\\pi}{4}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Tangent is positive in quadrants 1 and 3; its solutions are $\\pi$ apart.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x&=\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\pi=\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q30",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{4\\pi}{3},\\ \\frac{5\\pi}{3}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$. Sine is negative in quadrants 3 and 4.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\pi+\\frac{\\pi}{3}=\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\\\x&=2\\pi-\\frac{\\pi}{3}=\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q31",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\ \\frac{11\\pi}{6}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Cosine is positive in quadrants 1 and 4.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\\\x&=2\\pi-\\frac{\\pi}{6}=\\frac{11\\pi}{6}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q32",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\tan x=-\\sqrt3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{2\\pi}{3},\\ \\frac{5\\pi}{3}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$. Tangent is negative in quadrants 2 and 4; its solutions are $\\pi$ apart.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\pi-\\frac{\\pi}{3}=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}+\\pi=\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
